WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.133
-Henry Winkler. I want to talk about "Barry."

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.868
-What do you want to talk about? -This season.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.300
-James Fallon, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.834
-I want to talk about how good you are.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.801
Can we talk about your career on TikTok?

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:14.634
-[ Gasps ] Well, you know, it started because my granddaughter

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.501
said, "Oh, Papa, you have to make a TikTok."

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.000
So we made a TikTok one Christmas.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.634
Then the second Christmas, we made a TikTok.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:26.133
And then I put the phone in the refrigerator because I thought

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:30.567
it was the coldest place in the house, in California.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.467
And I, you know -- For a "happy new year."

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.801
Which is, like, you know, snowy and --

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.434
And so I opened the refrigerator.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:40.501
You heard the chili and the ketchup clink.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.834
And I just wished everybody a happy new year.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:46.501
And then I made a TikTok with my newest granddaughter.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.534
Our newest granddaughter, Francis Joan.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.567
I sang her "The Apple Song" that I wrote.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.234
-Yeah. How does "The Apple Song" --

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.767
-Do you want to hear it? -I would love to hear it.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.901
Would you like to?

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.634
-Thank you.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.100
Maybe I should stand for it.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.467
-Yeah.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:05.200
-♪ Apples are red and apples are green ♪

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.601
♪ And some are yellow ♪

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.100
♪♪

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.701
-That's my new favorite -- -Tariq!

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.300
-That's my new favorite song.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.234
You got a "Tariq!"

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:27.701
Not only are you a phenomenal actor and just a great person.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:28.801
-Thank you!

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.100
-Gosh, I love your wife, Stacey, too.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.100
So much, by the way. Really, I'm in love with her.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.934
She is unbelievable. -Yeah. Live with her.

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.534
-You've written --

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:37.434
You've crushed the children's book game.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:40.200
-And our newest one is coming out next year,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.834
about a little duckling, a baby little duckling.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.133
Lives on a pond in New Hampshire,

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.400
and she dreams about being a detective.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.133
Tariq! -Hey! You have -- Now --

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.267
But now you're writing --

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.000
Henry, you're writing your memoir.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.734
-But you know what? I am so nervous about it.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.100
I don't know what to write.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.300
I thought maybe there would be a chapter of --

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.300
someone would yell out a celebrity,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.567
you know, like, "Kareem Abdul-Jabbar!"

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:12.801
Oh, so, I was in the locker room in the '80s.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:16.367
He threw me his jersey after a game, and I didn't know --

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:18.300
I didn't know he was giving it to me,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.567
so I threw it in the hamper.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.400
-What?! You could have had his jersey?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.100
-I could have had the jersey.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.868
I put it in the laundry.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.167
-This is real? -So real.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.033
-If I name a name, could you have a story?

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.801
-Go ahead. Give me a name.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.601
-Lady Gaga. -Lady Gaga!

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:36.400
Okay, so, at NBC, I'm at a party.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.601
She's sitting there at the table.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:41.934
I love this woman. Great, talented.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.434
And I walk up to her, and, of course,

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:48.634
I trip over my own foot, and I fall in front of her.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:49.801
"Hi."

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:54.767
And then I just kind of slinked out of the restaurant.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.934
-Yeah. Cher. -Cher.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.634
Cher called me once and invited me --

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.100
-This is amazing. -No, truly.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.868
-These are real stories? -Real stories.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:05.167
She invited me -- She used to have great

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:06.901
skating parties in L.A.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.567
-Okay. -So, she called me up

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.734
and she said, "Can I talk to Henry?"

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.934
I said, "Hi. This is Henry."

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:15.534
She said, "You don't sound like Henry."

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.033
I said, "No, no, no, it is Henry."

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:20.934
She thought I was the Fonz. -Of course.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.133
We all thought you were the Fonz.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.567
-You did? -Well, you are the Fonz.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.400
-[As the Fonz] Alright. Then don't look me in the eye.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.067
-[ Laughs ] Wow! Yes!

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.400
-Hey! -That's it right there.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.300
That's exactly right!

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.501
So, Cher calls you and says...

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.934
[as Cher] "You don't sound like..."

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.734
-Yes. She sounded like that.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:43.667
-"You don't sound like Henry." -That's true.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:47.300
♪ You don't sound like you are the Fonz ♪

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.601
-[Normal voice] She said that? -She said that.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.767
I could not imitate her the way you did.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.300
-[ Laughs ] I probably couldn't.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.734
And did you go to the roller-skating party?

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.834
-I did not because I was embarrassed.

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:02.501
-Really? -Yes. Because I'm not a skater.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:04.868
-And the Fonz wasn't a roller skater, was he?

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.200
-No, he wasn't.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:11.367
There was one episode where I had to go with Potsy,

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.167
to do anything he wanted 'cause he did me a favor.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.400
-Yeah. -And he took me skating.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.300
And, you know, I was, like, out here and I was holding on.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.033
-[ Laughs ] That's so good.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.434
I gotta say "Barry" --

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:27.033
-I think I just pulled something.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.234
-We just heard a sound effect. Yeah.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.968
-Questlove, I want to just say that documentary was amazing!

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.534
-Yeah, it was great. -Thank you.

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:34.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.734
-It was great.

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:41.000
You do the show "Barry," and you win an Emmy for it.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.667
And we all loved it. Oh, my gosh.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.267
You know everyone loves you.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.067
So -- But the acting was fantastic.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.801
You were great, and Bill Hader was great.

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.367
But this season... -He's genius.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:54.801
-...you took a -- you took it to a new level of acting.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.234
-Well, first of all, if it ain't on the page,

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.734
it ain't on the stage. -Okay.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:02.968
-So the writing -- Alec Berg and Bill and the --

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:07.033
And Liz and Duffy and all of the writers are amazing.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.767
-And what you got to do with this character.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.133
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.801
And I want to say this Sunday is the final, right,

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.601
of the third season. -Yep.

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:20.267
-And I'm -- I'm willing to go so far to say there is a scene

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.067
that might be the most intense work

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.534
I have ever done

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.701
since the beginning of my career in 1970.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.267
-Really? -Yes.

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:32.200
-And how is that -- -And Bill took me there.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.200
And I worked with an actor that was just introduced last week,

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.167
Robert Wisdom, who plays the love of my life,

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.834
who Bill killed.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:43.400
-Yes, that's right.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.133
In the show. Yeah, of course.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.834
-Stacey is backstage. -Of course. Yes. In "Barry."

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:53.400
-He plays her father.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.167
-Oof. Buddy. -Yeah.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.801
-Does Bill warn you when you do these scenes?

00:05:57.801 --> 00:06:00.701
-No. He just --

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:03.667
You know, he just takes me to the place.

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.868
-Really? -He -- I'm not kidding.

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:08.434
Because at home, I rehearse the scene.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.234
I think I've got it down.

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:14.434
And then I get to the set and I realize I was in Peru,

00:06:14.434 --> 00:06:17.467
and he would like me in Bangladesh.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:20.534
He takes me to a place I had never thought of.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:22.434
-[ Laughs ] I love how you put it that way.

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.067
This is all gonna go in the memoir.

00:06:24.067 --> 00:06:26.801
I can't wait to read this thing. I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:28.701
-Do you want to write it?

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:32.133
-[ Laughs ] Yes, I do. Tariq!

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:35.634
Here is Henry Winkler in "Barry." Take a look at this.

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:38.667
-Ooh! -No, no, no. Don't laugh.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.133
Keep it going, kids.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.334
-Ooh-ooh!

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.701
-Now, how do you feel? -Like a ghost.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:45.033
-Wrong. How do you feel?

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.434
-Embarrassed? -She's right.

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:48.767
Okay. Now do the scene.

00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:53.033
-Doctor, the generators are down.

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:55.100
If we don't get electricity back in the park,

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.467
the dinosaurs will escape.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:57.701
-Let's split up. -Stop.

00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.267
Alright. Do you see the difference?

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:02.501
Huh? It is all in the body. It's much more real.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.400
Now I believe she's got the code.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.734
He's gonna ride the dinosaur. It's all gonna be fine.

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:09.400
You've got to embrace your embarrassment.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.934
"I want a lollipop! I want it to be purple!"

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.767
Do I look like a fool? Not my problem.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.834
-Now, that's how you do it!

00:07:17.834 --> 00:07:19.868
That's how you do it! Henry Winkler!

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:21.701
Check out the season finale of "Barry"

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:23.868
this Sunday on HBO and HBO Max.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:26.634
You smell great, by the way. You're a stud.

